meta {
  name: Add Firehose
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: https://webexapis.com/v1/webhooks
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
  ~Authorization: Bearer {{personalAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "all",
    "targetUrl": "{{webhookTargetUrl}}",
    "resource": "all",
    "event": "all"
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: 0
  forwardAuthorizationHeader: false
}

docs {
  Creates the broadest possible "firehose" webhook — every resource, every event — the Create a
  Webhook endpoint with no scoping applied.

  **Body** (`body:json`)
  - `name` — a human-readable label for the webhook.
  - `targetUrl` — where Webex POSTs event notifications. Bound to the collection variable
    `{{webhookTargetUrl}}`; replace with your own receiving endpoint.
  - `resource` — `all` subscribes to every resource type Webex supports webhooks for (messages,
    memberships, calls, meetings, etc), not just Calling.
  - `event` — `all` subscribes to every event type for those resources.

  **Usage note**: this is intentionally the noisiest possible webhook, useful for exploring what
  events exist during a demo. For production use, prefer the narrower "Add Firehose Calls" (scoped
  to Calling) or "Add All Created Calls" (scoped to one event type) as templates.

  Reference: https://developer.webex.com/docs/api/v1/webhooks/create-a-webhook

  ---
  *Documentation written by AI (Claude) as a companion to the WebexOne 2026 API Overview session.*
}
